# 02 — NEW ART DIRECTION

## The new design direction

WORLD SIGNAL should become:

**A Contemporary Global Affairs Journal — Editorial Energy × Evidence Clarity.**

It should combine:

- The visual storytelling ambition of The Washington Post.
- The typographic refinement of The New Yorker.
- The information architecture of the Financial Times.
- The international magazine atmosphere of Monocle.
- The editorial consistency of The Economist.
- The visual experimentation of The Pudding.

The result must have its own identifiable personality.

I do not want a traditional newspaper clone.

I do not want a generic SaaS dashboard.

I do not want a minimalist documentation website.

I do not want an excessively dark interface consisting of identical panels.

I do not want generic AI landing-page aesthetics.

I want a sophisticated digital publication with a strong visual identity.

## The most important shift

The previous direction overemphasized restraint and imposed too many visual prohibitions.

The result is clean, but often visually quiet.

Replace that approach with:

**Purposeful Visual Energy.**

Allow strong composition, contrasting typography, carefully selected imagery, meaningful color, expressive illustrations, different visual densities, and carefully designed interactions.

Restraint should improve the design, not eliminate its personality.

