# 11 — DESIGN RULES: WHAT MUST CHANGE

Do not blindly preserve the restrictive visual rules of the old Phase 03 art direction.

Replace the old idea of zero decorative expression with purposeful visual design.

Specifically:

- Do not force every component into the same rectangular panel.
- Do not use hairline separators for every section.
- Do not make all typography small and subdued.
- Do not restrict all visual accents to a tiny vermilion marker.
- Do not use generic metadata strips as the primary source of visual detail.
- Do not turn every image into a small framed thumbnail.
- Do not force the entire design to look like an archival document.
- Do not use dark backgrounds for every major content area.
- Do not make all three domain sections look like the same template with different colors.

Introduce intentional variation.

However:

- Avoid clutter.
- Preserve legibility.
- Preserve visual consistency.
- Preserve brand identity.
- Preserve semantic meaning.
- Preserve accessibility.

The goal is controlled visual richness.

